   "reply": "I added a `count` command that prints the number of notes, and the project checks pass: all 7 tests, with no line-length violations.\n\n- **Command:** `count` is handled in `fieldnotes/cli.py` and prints `len(store.load())`. I added it to the usage string too.\n- **Tests:** I added `CliCountTests` in `tests/test_store.py`. It checks that an empty store prints `0` and that two added notes print `2`, both with exit code 0.\n- **Checks:** I ran `python tools/check.py`. It requires `NOTES_HOME`, so I pointed it at a temporary directory instead of any real notes location.",
